  "title": "Madhava of Sangamagrama",
  "summary": "A mathematician-astronomer of Kerala who, around 1400 per MacTutor, found series equivalent to those for sine, cosine and arctangent and used them to compute pi to 11 decimal places. Almost nothing is certain about his life; his dates are given as c. 1340-1425 or 1350-1425, and the location of his home village Sangamagrama is disputed.",
